# Sibling git worktrees. `scripts/new-worktree.mjs` puts every one under
# .claude/worktrees/, so without this `format:check` walks into whatever every
# other agent currently has checked out and fails on THEIR in-progress files —
# a gate that reports someone else's work as this tree's problem is a gate
# people learn to ignore. ESLint already skips these: it ignores dot-directories
# by default, which is why only prettier saw them.
#
# Scoped to worktrees/ rather than all of .claude, so the tracked
# settings.local.json stays checked.
.claude/worktrees
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
